{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact readable-diff design head 75b64f9034b595ca70a11721dd7df0b5934ea991 on builder/readable-diff-design-20261102, for request 353a0ec0 and review request d2bb2da3.\n\nThe gap. The line gutters in the renders split three-digit line numbers across two lines. In ten-file.png, http-read.ts shows old line 355 as \"35\" over \"5\" and line 356 as \"35\" over \"6\", and ten-file-opened-light-320.png shows the same thing. truncated-light-592.png escapes it only because its open rows are lines 8 to 14. The cause is proposal.css: `.row` gives each gutter `3.5ch`, and `.old,.new` add `padding-right:6px`. At 12 px monospace, three digits plus the padding exceed 3.5ch, so the number wraps. The note says \"Separate old and new gutters preserve coordinates\", and the request's scene asks that additions, removals, context and hunk headers read apart at a glance. These are the renders Hugh will judge readability from, and they show wrong-looking coordinates on the one file the key render opens. The render matrix checks DOM rows, overflow and requests, but it does not check that a gutter number fits on one line, so the defect passed.\n\nTo close it, size each gutter to the widest line number the patch contains, or set a fixed width that holds the largest number in these fixtures, and keep `white-space:nowrap` on the gutter cells. Recapture the series and the three key renders. Add a render check that every gutter cell occupies one line box. The note can keep adaptive gutters as future implementation work, but the mockups need numbers that read correctly.\n\nEverything else meets 353a0ec0 under rulings 09a2b61a and a63f7698:\n\n- Scope. Main f277867f is an ancestor. The head adds one commit and fourteen paths, all under notes/. The worktree is clean. The static HTML holds no script. Every \"http\" match in it sits inside escaped repository code.\n- The renderer choice is measured. The corrected unmodified Pierre 1.6.2 vanilla text build emits 11,085,213 bytes, which is more than ten times the 1,048,576-byte resource cap. The disposable own probe emits 6,023 bytes, and TypeScript plus one dark Shiki theme brings it to 364,934. The note says that the probe does not estimate a finished renderer, and that syntax stays optional because it loses multiline state.\n- The under-claims survive. The interdiff keeps **Cannot separate from base change**, both version patches with their own endpoints, and \"Version 2 does not change this file.\" The truncated case keeps **Truncated** and the server's left-out words with every file collapsed, and it marks the partial patch. Collapsed, not received and omitted stay three separate states.\n- Provenance is labeled on every render. The ten-file and truncated code is byte-identical history held in labeled synthetic local commits, as 09a2b61a permits. The accepted J2 room stays untouched.\n- The budget work keeps the internal Projection and the outbound Display separate, measures the proposed substitutions, and labels them hypothetical.\n\nEvidence. The manifest hashes to 0bd248d0…f119bad008. All 267 files match, and all 24 table digests match the manifest. SHA256SUMS passes in the evidence and review directories, and the review directory's SHA256SUMS hashes to 04346078…288eebd2. Its four checks read \"exit 0\", no file is writable, and the credential-pattern scan finds nothing.\n\nStale bases. All three artifacts read as stale because the builder's question 6aa4f2c2 was withdrawn after the planner answered it in 09a2b61a. The answer still stands and is not retired, so the staleness changes nothing this review relies on.\n\nArchitecture: sound as a proposal. Structured files, hunks and rows, with completeness in the server and display folds local to the card, keep folding apart from omission. The opaque binding it proposes for a future range read is the right boundary. Security: no finding. Repository text enters text nodes, the read buttons are inactive, the pages make no outside request, and private fixture output stays outside the unit. Simplification: no required change beyond the gutter.\n\nLimits stay explicit: no product renderer, schema or dependency changes, no Goose Desktop claim (1a44f042), and the held cut-short answer stays with e4d0cfed. Hugh decides after landing and before any build.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3eae0f7d8e5fabc0935d5fcfd211f954b89b6bc9","binding":"assigned","head":"75b64f9034b595ca70a11721dd7df0b5934ea991","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c17e9f8bf58791ed92a94faa634f79d4b015282c\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5e63db87aa26c3d72b8c5a512fbb2fd83480cc47\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c17e9f8bf58791ed92a94faa634f79d4b015282c","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:023970667fe92917b223dd45fea41a0b16f74a82, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3aef9573118690c7170b684a6cf8ac7b19b7f71a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3eae0f7d8e5fabc0935d5fcfd211f954b89b6bc9, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c17e9f8bf58791ed92a94faa634f79d4b015282c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d2bb2da3d4dbc971bbcaaf3d2a1ad7bc74d1b55f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:009d3a2248bcb08ba19c4dcab5f584ecfd700ba3, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:099749a5a4e95a318e266c9c0992a4287ffa5122, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0f5ad1fc88f3de054223a44f45ffb459e5247ec2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:14b7265622f42dc2cf02bf6ccc17dc1167add858 and 45 more","staleness":"artifact, promise, request stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15